{
  "version": 1,
  "_provisional": [],
  "_evidence": "FINAL mapping for the AsiaGolfReview legacy import (agr-launch W2). No site id, no image host: those live in the owner-held overlay ~/agr-private/overlay.json. Decided 26-10-26 by the owner ('ok' to the six proposals) from the discovery result (01-discover-agr.sql run in the globaltravelpost SQL Editor 26-10-26: site asiagolfreview, 605 rows = 343 published, 208 archived (193 never published), 51 draft, 3 rejected; countries column empty on every row; 578 featured images on the old Supabase storage host, 27 none, 0 body images; no rankings, press-room or events-awards rows). (1) status: published only; archived, draft, scheduled, rejected are SKIP; catch-up runs before cutover pick up what the old site publishes after the first run. (2) categories: legacy subsections equal to a new sub-section pass through (destinations, itineraries, resorts-stays, players, tournament-news, watch-prize-money, club-management, data-insights, development-design, people); golf-travel/practical-game goes to the-practical-game; course-reviews/by-country goes to course-reviews with no sub-section (no country data, editors assign later); course-reviews/new-renovated and hidden-gems go to course-reviews with no sub-section plus the tag of the same name; gear-style/equipment and tested-in-tropics go to gear-style with no sub-section (editors assign clubs/balls/bags later); gear-style/style goes to apparel; the-game with an empty subsection resolves through the-game/*. Rankings, press-room entries stay for completeness (no rows today); events-awards has no entry on purpose (unmapped is reject). (3) authors: even split over the 5 staff names of the Team page by slug hash; legacy bylines are not kept. (4) tags: only the 7 approved tags survive (2380 legacy tags dropped). (5) media.bodyImages: drop (none exist). (6) archivedAs: section (301 to the article's section page, not 410). Old origin is the apex https://asiagolfreview.com; www also serves 200 today, so the cutover redirects cover both hosts. Pages without articles (/events-awards, /architects, /studio, /licensing, /press-room-submit, tool pages) get hand-written redirects in agr-web at cutover, not from this mapping.",
